NSLog - a variadic function: on arm64 Apple a variadic argument rides the stack, which a fixed prototype does not place
NSMaxRange - a static inline function: its body lives in the header and in no binary, so the interpreter needs a thin C stub (design §5 «Только в заголовке»)
NSStringFromRect - a function taking a struct CGRect by value as argument 1, which the bridge cannot carry
NSUIntegerMax - enumerator value is not representable in the underlying type 'long long'
NSWindowDidResizeNotification - a mutable pointer global (NSNotificationName _Nonnull): a pointer read once at load would not be its value later
kCFRunLoopDefaultMode - a raw pointer global (const CFRunLoopMode): what it points at has no owner the bridge can name, and releasing it would be a guess
